Java 21. Why does this `switch` compile without a `default`, and what happens if someone adds `record Tri(double b, double h) implements Shape` and lists it in `permits`?

```java
sealed interface Shape
    permits Circle, Rect {}
record Circle(double r)
    implements Shape {}
record Rect(double w, double h)
    implements Shape {}

double area(Shape s) {
  return switch (s) {
    case Circle c ->
        3.14 * c.r() * c.r();
    case Rect(double w, double h) ->
        w * h;
  };
}
```

